00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:05.990 align:start position:0%
among the features available  in deep chain we integrated a molecular  dynamics simulation tool  it allows users to simulate and  visualize  the molecular dynamics of protein  complexes  these full-scale gpu-powered simulations  compute the physical movements  of the molecules through time in the  context of protein complexes  the analysis of molecular dynamic  evolution can be informative  of their stability the md simulations  can be found in the upper right tab of  the workspace  new design can be created by either  uploading a local pdb file  or downloading one from the rcsb pdb  database  using a four letter code once your  design has been created  you can select it from the existing  designs panel  as the simulations for the molecular  dynamics can take several hours  we're going to load a design for which  the simulations have already been  computed  for the sake of the demo here we're  going to select a bone morphogenesis  protein complex we enter the md  simulations tab  running a simulation from our design's  native structure can be performed by  clicking this button  the number of minimization and  simulation steps  can be adjusted in the pop-up window  beforehand  in our case we can see here that a  molecular dynamic simulation for our  native protein complex has already  been launched and was completed  successfully the results of the  molecular dynamics simulation can now be  explored  the first panel is dedicated to the  parameters of the protein movements  visualization  by adjusting the two available sliders  the simulation can be viewed either  frame by frame  or played as a video with the speed of  your choice  below them you'll find a graph  displaying the evolution of the global  complex energy with time  thank you for watching and enjoy deep  chain
 

